 "reading": "The fit peaks at W=64. Raw MACs span 3.4x across the ladder but padded-64 MACs span only 1.6x, and latency spans 1.29x from the unpruned rung to the deepest one (1.30x between the slowest and fastest rungs -- latency is not monotone, lamp -10% sits above unpruned). Channels cut below the tile width cost accuracy and buy no time. NOTE the W=1 entry is this script's own raw-MAC fit, not the ladder's latency_law.r2 -- MACs are recounted here by tracing the model. Compare the peak against W=1 within this table. This is a whole-model fit; the layer-level corollary has NOT been tested at layer granularity.",
